<title>UK: UK's Major confirms 20 pct tax rate is his target.</title>
<headline>UK's Major confirms 20 pct tax rate is his target.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister John Major on Thursday confirmed that a 20 percent standard rate of income tax was a key aim of his government.</p>
<p>&quot;I can confirm our first priority is to move towards, when affordable, a 20p basic rate of tax,&quot; he said at Prime Minister's question time in parliament.  </p>
<p>Major said that after achieving this target, his next aims would be to move towards abolition of capital gains and inheritance taxes. -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
